### operation add [exit 0]
Add an operation: a protocol-independent contract, with an optional schema
for each input value and each output value. Leaving a schema out leaves that
side unspecified. Aliases are other names the operation answers to, such as a
shared contract's name for it.

Changes <obi> in place. Give - as <obi> to read a document from stdin and
print the result instead, or use --dry-run to see the change without
writing it.

Usage:
  ob operation add <obi> <name> [flags]

Examples:
  ob operation add tasks.obi.json archiveTask --description "Archive a task." \
      --input-schema '{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id"]}' \
      --output-schema '{"$ref":"#/schemas/Task"}'

Flags:
      --alias stringArray      another name the operation answers to (repeatable)
      --deprecated             mark the operation deprecated
      --description string     what the operation does
      --dry-run                show the change without writing it
  -h, --help                   help for add
      --input-schema string    schema for each input value: JSON, @file, or -
      --output-schema string   schema for each output value: JSON, @file, or -
      --tag stringArray        a documentation tag (repeatable)


